#==============================================================================================
#
#   fetching_6 - Fetch::Fetching: HTTP-network-or-cache fetch
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of Libraries/LibWeb/Fetch/Fetching/Fetching.cpp (lines 1559-2070):
#       HTTP-network-or-cache fetch: the HTTP request (a clone of the request unless no
#       traversable prompts and redirects error), credentials, Content-Length and the keepalive
#       limit, Referer, Origin, the Fetch metadata headers, User-Agent, the cache-mode headers,
#       Sec-GPC, Authorization from the URL's credentials, the HTTP cache partition and the
#       memory cache (off unless enabled), then the network fetch through the ResourceLoader
#       and the 401, 407 and 421 retries. Each C++ lambda is a capture struct with a static
#       function (DESIGN.md §2.7).
